<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-APN year net profit $26.54 million.</title>
<headline>RTRS-APN year net profit $26.54 million.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>	   (millions A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   57.26 vs 55.82</p>
<p>    Net profit		   26.54 vs 26.39</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)    4.8  vs 4.8</p>
<p>NOTE: Results are equity-accounted. Australian Provincial Newspapers Ltd publishes regional and rural newspapers and operates radio networks. It is about 49 percent owned by the family interests of Irish businessman Tony O'Reilly and his main media group Independent Newspapers Plc.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     8.30 vs 8.00</p>
<p>    Sales				  298.34 vs 252.28</p>
<p>    Other income			   6.05 vs 4.30</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   12.3  vs 13.2</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			 0.19 vs 0.24</p>
<p>Dividend is fully franked</p>
<p>Pay date April 23</p>
<p>Reg date April 16</p>
<p>    Tax				     12.27 vs 11.52</p>
<p>    Interest				17.86 vs 15.38</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   6.97 vs 7.20</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
